\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Theorem}
\title{The normalized paired conditional functional}
\date{2026-11-10}

\p{Let #{V=R\oplus E} and let #{K:V\to V} have invertible eliminated
compression #{D}, with Schur complement #{S}, as in
\ref{fdip-00IX}. Write #{\theta_K=-\bar\psi(K\psi)} and
#{\theta_S=-\bar\psi_R(S\psi_R)}. For every polynomial #{F} in the
paired generators, the \newvocab{normalized paired conditional functional} is
##{\mathcal E_R^K(F)
=(\det_E D)^{-1}\ue^{-\theta_S}J_E(F \ue^{\theta_K}).}
It is a \vocabk{normalized conditional functional}{fdip-00KV} onto
the retained paired algebra. The formula uses the invertibility of
#{D}. When #{K} is invertible, #{S} is invertible and
##{\omega_K(F)=\omega_S(\mathcal E_R^K(F)),}
where #{\omega_K(F)=J_V(F \ue^{\theta_K})/\det K}. For a polynomial in
the retained generators, #{\mathcal E_R^K(F)=F}, and the identity
specializes to #{\omega_K(F)=\omega_S(F)}.}

\proof{
\p{The exponential is a sum of even elements. An even element
commutes with every homogeneous element, by the
[Grassmann algebra](fdip-008F). The eliminated top degree is even,
so moving an eliminated top word past a retained homogeneous factor
contributes no sign. Thus #{J_E(bF)=bJ_E(F)} and
#{J_E(Fb)=J_E(F)b} for retained #{b}, including odd #{b}. The
zero-source case of \ref{fdip-00IX} gives
##{J_E(\ue^{\theta_K})=\det_E(D)\,\ue^{\theta_S}.}
The right-hand side is an even central unit. Its inverse is
#{(\det_E D)^{-1}\ue^{-\theta_S}}, and therefore
#{\mathcal E_R^K(1)=1}. Retained factors pull out of #{J_E} and
commute with this inverse. For retained #{F}, the same formula
collapses to #{\mathcal E_R^K(F)=F}.}

\p{If #{K} is invertible, then #{\det K=\det(D)\det S} and #{S} is
invertible. For every polynomial #{F},
##{\mathcal E_R^K(F)\,\ue^{\theta_S}
=(\det_E D)^{-1}J_E(F \ue^{\theta_K}),}
because #{\ue^{\theta_S}} cancels its inverse. Applying #{J_R} and
dividing by #{\det S} produces
#{\omega_S(\mathcal E_R^K(F))=J_V(F \ue^{\theta_K})/\det K},
since #{J_RJ_E=J_V}. The scalar conventions of the empty blocks
remain those of the partial formula.}
}

\p{No Mathlib declaration was found for this normalized Grassmann
restriction. The identities use no norm on the algebra, and they do
not identify the Grassmann state with a state on the configuration
Clifford algebra.}

\p{Remark. The identity #{\det K=\det(D)\det S} is the factorization
of the action on the top exterior power. For the eliminated Grassmann
block, that reading is the remark in \ref{fdip-009J}.}
